<section id="about" class="section about">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section">About</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="about__prose">
      <p>
        I didn't arrive at this from theory. At the NBA I built the score strip with tens of
        millions of eyeballs on it. I co-founded Bar Savvy and ran it as CTO, often as its only
        engineer. I've done that alongside my work at LV Collective, where I now spend as much time
        teaching AI as I do building.
      </p>
      <p>
        I build this way for one reason: it lets a small team move like a much larger one, without
        the mess that usually comes with moving fast. It's why a deploy that used to eat the better
        part of an hour now takes about a minute, and why the people I hand this to start shipping
        work they couldn't before. The harness is what makes the speed safe enough to trust.
      </p>
      <p>
        I like being at the front of this. I like even more that the things I build actually run.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

